@startuml Checkout Flow with Inventory Reservation

title Checkout Flow với Inventory Reservation & Race Condition Prevention

actor Guest
participant "CheckoutController" as Controller
participant "CheckoutService" as Service
participant "InventoryReservationService" as ReservationService
participant "ProductVariantRepository" as VariantRepo
database "Database\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB
participant "OrderService" as OrderService
participant "EmailService" as EmailService

== Phase 1: Initiate Checkout & Reserve Inventory ==

Guest -> Controller: POST /api/checkout/initiate?cartId={uuid}
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: initiateCheckout(cartId)
activate Service

Service -> Service: Validate cart exists\nand has items

Service -> ReservationService: reserveInventory(cartItems)
activate ReservationService

note over ReservationService, DB
  **Race Condition Prevention**
  Sử dụng Pessimistic Locking
  để xử lý concurrent requests
end note

loop For each cart item
    ReservationService -> VariantRepo: findByIdWithLock(variantId)
    activate VariantRepo
    
    VariantRepo -> DB: SELECT * FROM product_variants\nWHERE id = ?\n**FOR UPDATE** (Row Lock)
    activate DB
    
    note right of DB
      **Pessimistic Lock Acquired**
      Transaction holds lock until commit
      Other transactions wait here
    end note
    
    DB --> VariantRepo: Locked ProductVariant
    deactivate DB
    
    VariantRepo --> ReservationService: ProductVariant (locked)
    deactivate VariantRepo
    
    ReservationService -> ReservationService: Calculate Available Stock\n= PhysicalStock - ActiveReservations
    
    alt Stock Available
        ReservationService -> DB: INSERT INTO inventory_reservation\n(session_id, variant_id, quantity,\nstatus='ACTIVE', expires_at=NOW()+15min)
        activate DB
        DB --> ReservationService: Reservation Created
        deactivate DB
        
        note right of ReservationService
          Reservation expires in 15 minutes
          Status: ACTIVE
        end note
        
    else Insufficient Stock
        ReservationService -> DB: ROLLBACK TRANSACTION
        activate DB
        DB --> ReservationService: Transaction Rolled Back
        deactivate DB
        
        ReservationService --> Service: throw InsufficientStockException
        Service --> Controller: Error Response
        Controller --> Guest: 400 Bad Request\n{"error": "Insufficient stock",\n"unavailableItems": [...]}
        
        note right of Guest
          Checkout failed
          Show error to user
        end note
        
        deactivate ReservationService
        deactivate Service
        deactivate Controller
        
        [<-- Guest: End (Failure)
    end
end

ReservationService -> DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
activate DB

note right of DB
  **Lock Released**
  Other waiting transactions
  can now proceed
end note

DB --> ReservationService: Transaction Committed
deactivate DB

ReservationService --> Service: Reservations Created\n(sessionId, expiresAt)
deactivate ReservationService

Service --> Controller: CheckoutSessionResponse\n(sessionId, expiresAt)
deactivate Service

Controller --> Guest: 200 OK\n{"sessionId": "uuid",\n"expiresAt": "timestamp"}
deactivate Controller

note right of Guest
  Guest has 15 minutes
  to complete checkout
end note

== Phase 2: Guest Fills Shipping Info ==

Guest -> Guest: Fill shipping information\n(name, phone, email, address)\nSelect payment method\n(COD or Bank Transfer)

== Phase 3: Confirm Checkout & Create Order ==

Guest -> Controller: POST /api/checkout/confirm?sessionId={id}\nBody: {customerInfo, paymentMethod}
activate Controller

Controller -> Service: confirmCheckout(sessionId, checkoutRequest)
activate Service

Service -> Service: Validate session exists\nand not expired

Service -> OrderService: createOrder(session, checkoutRequest)
activate OrderService

OrderService -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
activate DB

OrderService -> DB: INSERT INTO orders\n(tracking_number, customer_info,\ntotal_amount, payment_method,\nstatus='PENDING')
DB --> OrderService: Order Created

OrderService -> DB: INSERT INTO order_items\n(order_id, variant_id, quantity,\nprice_at_purchase)
DB --> OrderService: Order Items Created

OrderService -> VariantRepo: Deduct Physical Stock
activate VariantRepo

VariantRepo -> DB: UPDATE product_variants\nSET physical_stock = physical_stock - quantity\nWHERE id = ?
DB --> VariantRepo: Stock Updated
deactivate VariantRepo

OrderService -> ReservationService: Mark Reservations as COMPLETED
activate ReservationService

ReservationService -> DB: UPDATE inventory_reservation\nSET status = 'COMPLETED'\nWHERE session_id = ?
DB --> ReservationService: Reservations Completed
deactivate ReservationService

OrderService -> DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
DB --> OrderService: Transaction Committed
deactivate DB

note right of OrderService
  Order created successfully
  Stock deducted
  Reservations completed
end note

OrderService -> EmailService: sendOrderConfirmation(order)
activate EmailService

EmailService -> Guest: Email: Order Confirmation\nTracking Number: {uuid}\nTracking URL: {baseUrl}/track/{uuid}
deactivate EmailService

OrderService --> Service: Order
deactivate OrderService

Service -> Service: Mark cart as CONVERTED

Service --> Controller: OrderResponse\n(orderId, trackingNumber)
deactivate Service

Controller --> Guest: 200 OK\n{"orderId": "uuid",\n"trackingNumber": "uuid",\n"status": "PENDING"}
deactivate Controller

note right of Guest
  Checkout completed
  Order created
  Email sent
end note

== Alternative Flow: Reservation Expires ==

... 15 minutes later ...

participant "ScheduledJob" as Scheduler

Scheduler -> ReservationService: cleanupExpiredReservations()
activate Scheduler
activate ReservationService

ReservationService -> DB: UPDATE inventory_reservation\nSET status = 'EXPIRED'\nWHERE created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '15 minutes'\nAND status = 'ACTIVE'
activate DB

DB --> ReservationService: X reservations expired
deactivate DB

ReservationService --> Scheduler: Cleanup completed
deactivate ReservationService
deactivate Scheduler

note right of Scheduler
  Expired reservations
  no longer count toward
  available stock calculation
end note

@enduml
